# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fork-specific environment variables for the laode production deployment.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file is FORK-EXCLUSIVE (upstream's NostalgiaForInfinity does not have it)
# so it never conflicts on rebase. It documents only the env vars this fork adds
# on top of upstream's live-account-example.env. Set these in your deployment
# platform (e.g. Dokploy) alongside the vars documented upstream.
#
# Rule: NEVER edit a file that also exists in upstream (it causes rebase
# conflicts). If you need to customize an upstream file, copy it to a new
# fork-exclusive filename and document the divergence here.

# ─── Webhook → freqtrade-notifier ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The freqtrade-notifier service requires a shared secret on every webhook.
# Freqtrade's webhook sender cannot set custom Authorization/x-api-key headers,
# so the secret rides in the URL as ?key=. The value MUST match the notifier's
# WEBHOOK_API_KEY env var exactly.
#
# Generate a secret: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
FREQTRADE__WEBHOOK__URL=https://freqtrade-notifier.lamualfa.dev/webhook/freqtrade?key=Put_Your_Notifier_Webhook_Key_Here
